summary.value:
EchoShot is a system for multi-shot portrait video generation with subject-identity consistency and shot-wise controllability. Built on a 1.3 B-parameter Wan-DiT backbone, the framework introduces two shot-aware rotary-position-embedding variants: Temporal-Cut RoPE (TcRoPE) for marking inter-shot boundaries in self-attention and Temporal-Align RoPE (TaRoPE) for suppressing cross-shot leakage in text-video cross-attention.Training is driven by PortraitGala, a newly curated 600 k-clip dataset (400 k identities, 1 k h video) with fine-grained captions Three tasks are demonstrated:
MT2V - text-to-multi-shot video;
PMT2V - personalised multi-shot generation from a face reference;
InfT2V - unbounded shot extension via a disentangled RefAttn.

On a private 100-prompt benchmark,  EchoShot improves identity consistency and prompt alignment over keyframe pipelines and HunyuanVideo, while users prefer its outputs in >70 % pairwise votes. All code and data are promised for open-source release upon acceptance

